      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 651391887,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Unfortunately this approach is too simple. TCP, being a streaming protocol, does not guarantee that any segment contains a single and complete RADIUS PDU. You would need to add a function which, together with TCP dissector helper, can find those boundaries and hand that over to dissect_radius(). See the Wireshark Developer Guide, [section 9.5](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsdg_html_chunked/ChDissectReassemble.html#TcpDissectPdus) on this.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2398962,
            "username": "JaapKeuter",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jaap Keuter",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/722b0c520542a23cb8f8ea7070a45c88f9e9214dc700ac151e419e9649e0304e?s=80&d=identicon",
